  "major": "history-ba-nyc-cb9d5662",
  "major_name": "History",
  "degree": "BA",
  "campus": "New York",
  "college": "College of Social Sciences and Humanities",
  "overview_text": "The Bachelor of Arts is a broadly based liberal arts degree in history. Students who pursue the BA degree must satisfy general requirements and take courses to satisfy Northeastern's universitywide core curriculum ( NUpath ), in addition to required and elective history courses. These requirements help students develop their historical knowledge and skills within the contexts of the arts, humanities, social sciences, and sciences that together comprise the disciplinary sources of historical knowledge. The curriculum enables historical understanding to be culturally and linguistically sensitive to the subjects of historical inquiry. This program is currently only available to former Marymount Manhattan College students who are eligible for continued enrollment at Northeastern University. This program includes required courses that will be taught on ground at the Northeastern New York City campus.",
  "source_text": "Complete all courses listed below unless otherwise indicated. Also complete any corequisite labs, recitations, clinicals, or tools courses where specified and complete any additional courses needed beyond specific college and major requirements to satisfy graduation credit requirements.\nUniversitywide Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nUniversitywide Requirements\n.\nBA Language Requirements\nAll BA students are required to complete the BA degree language requirements, for a total of 12 semester hours of language study or demonstrated equivalent proficiency, as described in\nAdditional Requirements for BA students\n. Successful demonstration of proficiency does not reduce total minimum semester hours of study required to earn the BA degree.\nNUpath Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nNUpath Requirements\n.\nNew York State Liberal Arts and Sciences Requirements\nAll undergraduate students enrolled in programs at the New York campus are required to fulfill\nNew York State Liberal Arts and Sciences requirements\n.\nHistory Major Requirements\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nIntroductory History\nHIST 1000\nHistory at Northeastern\n1\nHistorical Research and Writing\nHIST 1200\nHistorical Research and Writing\n1\nHIST 1201\nFirst-Year Seminar\n4\nHistory Seminar and Historical Writing\nHIST 2301\nThe History Seminar\n4\nHIST 2302\nHistorical Writing\n1\nAdditional History Requirements\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nPre-1800 Course\nComplete one of the following:\n4\nHIST 1100\nLaw and History\nHIST 2330\nColonial and Revolutionary America\nHIST 2370\nRenaissance to Enlightenment\nHIST 2390\nAfrica and the World in Early Times\nHIST 3334\nAssassinations in World History\nHistory Outside the United States and Europe\nComplete one of the following:\n4\nHIST 1150\nEast Asian Studies\nHIST 1290\nModern Middle East\nHIST 1500\nModern China\nHIST 2211\nThe World Since 1945\nHIST 2311\nColonialism/Imperialism\nHIST 2351\nModern Japan\nCapstone\nHIST 4701\nCapstone Seminar\n4\nHistory Electives\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nComplete additional HIST courses not used to fulfill a previous requirement.\nGeneral History Elective Requirement\nComplete three HIST courses at any level in any field.\n12\nIntermediate/Advanced Course Requirement\nComplete a minimum of one HIST course numbered 2000 to 2999 (excluding\nHIST 2301\nand\nHIST 2302\n).\n4\nAdvanced Course Requirement\nComplete a minimum of two HIST courses numbered 3000 to 4999 (excluding\nHIST 4701\n).\n8\nHistory Major Credit Requirement\nComplete 46 semester hours in the major.\nExperiential Liberal Arts Requirement\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nComplete one of the following:\nANTH 3410\nEthnographic Field Experience\nECON 2350\nStatistics for Economists\nENGL 3340\nTechnologies of Text\nENGL 3381\nThe Practice and Theory of Teaching Writing\nENGL 3382\nPublishing in the 21st Century\nENGL 3400\nOpening the Archive\nHIST 1120\nPublic History, Public Memory\nHIST 2311\nColonialism/Imperialism\nHUSV 1101\nSocial Change and Human Services\nSOCL 2485\nEnvironment, Technology, and Society\nOptional Co-op\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nSuccessful completion of EXED 2000 is required for participation in co-op.\nEXED 2000\nProfessional Development for Co-op\n1\nCOOP 3945\nCo-op Work Experience\n0\nor\nCOOP 3946\nCo-op Work Experience--Half Time\nor\nCOOP 3947\nCo-op Work Experience Abroad--Half Time\nor\nCOOP 3948\nCo-op Work Experience Abroad\nProgram Requirements\n128 total semester hours required",
